   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "L04B_001_Square With Type Hints",
   "display_name": "Square With Type Hints",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>So far, when you defined a function, you never said what <b>type</b> of value each parameter should be, or what type the function returns. Python doesn't force you to say this - but it's very good practice to do so anyway, using <b>type hints</b>.</p>\n<pre>def square_it(a: int) -> int:\n    return a * a</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>a: int</code> tells anyone reading the code (including you, later!) that <code>a</code> is meant to be an <code>int</code>. The <code>-&gt; int</code> after the parentheses tells us the function is meant to <b>return</b> an <code>int</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Important:</b> type hints are just documentation - Python does <b>not</b> actually enforce them at runtime. If you passed in a string by mistake, Python wouldn't stop you. But they make your code far easier to understand at a glance, and many code editors use them to catch mistakes before you even run your code.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Complete the function <code>square_it</code> below (its type-hinted signature is already provided) so that it returns the square of <code>a</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>square_it(5)</code> should return <code>25</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def square_it(a: int) -> int:\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(square_it(5))",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(square_it(5))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "25",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(square_it(0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(square_it(-3))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "9",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
