   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L04B_003_Average With Float Hints",
   "display_name": "Average With Float Hints",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Type hints work the same way for <code>float</code> parameters and return types.</p>\n<pre>def average_of_two(a: float, b: float) -> float:\n    return (a + b) / 2</pre>\n<p><b>Reminder:</b> since this returns a float, round it with <code>round(value, 2)</code> before returning, to avoid tiny floating-point mismatches.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Complete the function <code>average_of_two</code> below (its type-hinted signature is already provided) so that it returns the average of <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>, rounded to 2 decimal places.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>average_of_two(3.0, 4.0)</code> should return <code>3.5</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def average_of_two(a: float, b: float) -> float:\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(average_of_two(3.0, 4.0))",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(average_of_two(3.0, 4.0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3.5",
