  {
   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "L04B_006_List Sum With List Hint",
   "display_name": "List Sum With List Hint",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A parameter that's meant to be a list can be hinted with <code>list</code>, the same way you'd hint <code>int</code> or <code>str</code>.</p>\n<pre>def list_sum(lst: list) -> int:\n    total = 0\n    for value in lst:\n        total = total + value\n    return total</pre>\n<p>This tells us <code>list_sum</code> expects a <code>list</code> argument, and returns an <code>int</code> (the sum).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Complete the function <code>list_sum</code> below (its type-hinted signature is already provided) so that it returns the sum of the elements of <code>lst</code>, using a loop.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>list_sum([4, 8, 15, 16, 23])</code> should return <code>66</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def list_sum(lst: list) -> int:\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(list_sum([4, 8, 15, 16, 23]))",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
